From: ROG5 build <klimovich008@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] screen-saver-manager: Sync LockedHint once the session proxy
 exists

Phosh locks in main() before the screen saver manager has its logind
session proxy, and on_lockscreen_manager_locked_changed() only tells logind
when the proxy exists. So the startup lock never reached logind: LockedHint
stayed "no" on a locked phone until the next lock/unlock change. Anything
that trusts LockedHint (here: the ROG5 desktop-mode switcher, which must not
start an unlocked desktop from a locked phone) sees a locked phone as
unlocked. Sync the current state when the proxy arrives.
---
--- a/src/screen-saver-manager.c	2026-09-30 03:26:06.849063369 +0200
+++ b/src/screen-saver-manager.c	2026-09-30 03:26:06.866182450 +0200
@@ -675,6 +675,11 @@
     "swapped-object-signal::lock", G_CALLBACK (on_logind_lock), self,
     "swapped-object-signal::unlock", G_CALLBACK (on_logind_unlock), self,
     NULL);
+
+  /* The shell may have locked before we had the session proxy (phosh locks
+   * in main() before the screen saver manager exists), so that change never
+   * reached logind and LockedHint stayed "no" on a locked phone. Sync it. */
+  on_lockscreen_manager_locked_changed (self);
 }
 
 
